"""Long-form article — Best Roof Racks for 2018–2026 Jeep Wrangler JL (2-door and 4-door Unlimited).
Mirrors the approved pilot (ford_f150_2021_tonneau.py) and the roof-rack guides (4Runner, Bronco, Tahoe).
No invented hands-on testing. Vehicle facts come from Jeep's 2018 Wrangler launch release on Stellantis Media
(Sky One-Touch powertop, Sunrider soft top, body-color and black three-piece hardtops, "Lighter Freedom panels",
trim list by door count, "a roof rack for mounting Mopar carriers" as a Mopar accessory) and Wikipedia's JL page
(96.8 / 118.4 in wheelbases, 166.8 / 188.4 in lengths, production from November 2017, JK built until April 27, 2018,
2024 refresh), both opened 2026-10-05. Product specs come from the maker or retailer pages in SOURCES (Rough Country
configurator and ExtremeTerrain for 10612, Dometic for the Front Runner 1/2 kit, CB Adventure Supply for the Front
Runner Extreme kit, Rhino-Rack for RJLB1 and ExtremeTerrain for JB0880, Hooke Road for HE.3057-S, TrailFX and The
Engine Block for JL012T). Amazon picks are identified by listing title read in amazon.com search results; amazon.com
pages cannot be fetched, so where a spec comes only from a title the page says so. No Jeep roof load figure was read;
the page says so and sends readers to the owner's manual. No pick on this page is listed by its maker for a soft top;
the page says so.
"""

