FAQ = [
 ("What is the best roof rack for a 2018–2026 Jeep Wrangler JL?",
  "For most 4-door owners, the Rough Country 10612. Rough Country lists it at $729.95 for the 2018–2026 JL, rates it at 225 lb dynamic and 450 lb static evenly distributed, and calls it Freedom Panel compatible on 4-door models with a 100% bolt-on install and no drilling. It is excluded on Jeeps with the Sky One-Touch power top. If you want a flat aluminum tray with no drilling, the Front Runner Slimline II 1/2 kit mounts to the hardtop gutters. If you have a 2-door hardtop, the Hooke Road rack at $299.99 is the one made for your roof. If you only carry a kayak or a cargo box, a crossbar set is enough."),
 ("Does the Wrangler JL have factory roof rails?",
  "No. Jeep's 2018 launch release lists three roofs, the Sky One-Touch powertop, the Sunrider soft top and the three-piece hardtop with Freedom panels, and never mentions roof rails. The only factory mention of a rack is that Mopar introduced \"a roof rack for mounting Mopar carriers\" as an accessory; we did not find a current Mopar page or an Amazon listing for it, so ask a dealer. Everything on this page therefore attaches to the hardtop itself, to its drip gutters, or to the Jeep's body. That is the opposite of a 4Runner or a Tahoe, where the rails do the work and the bars just clamp on."),
 ("Can I put a roof rack on a Wrangler soft top?",
  "Not with any pick on this page. The Sunrider soft top is fabric over bows and cannot carry a load, and none of the makers here list their rack for a soft top. Rough Country's page addresses the hardtop and Freedom panels and excludes the Sky One-Touch; TrailFX's page says only that its rack bolts to factory mounting points. If you run a soft top, ask Rough Country or TrailFX in writing whether the rack can be used with the top up and down before you buy, or plan on a hitch cargo carrier instead. Our 2018–2026 Wrangler hitch guide covers the receiver you would need."),
 ("Which racks fit the 2-door Wrangler JL?",
  "Fewer than fit the Unlimited, because the 2-door hardtop is much shorter. Wikipedia's JL page lists a 96.8 in wheelbase and 166.8 in length for the 2-door against 118.4 in and 188.4 in for the 4-door. Hooke Road's HE.3057-S is built for the 2018–2026 2-door hardtop. Front Runner sells a 2-door Slimline II 1/2 kit on Amazon. Rough Country lists the 10612 for both bodies but warns that it will hinder removing the Freedom panels on 2-door models. The 200 lb crossbar set here names 2-door and 4-door Jeeps. Every other pick is 4-door only."),
 ("Can I still take the Freedom panels off with a rack installed?",
  "It depends on the rack. Rough Country calls the 10612 Freedom Panel compatible on 4-door models and says it hinders panel removal on 2-doors. Hooke Road says the front top panels \"can be easily removed and installed\" once its 2-door rack is on, because the rack covers the rear of the top. Front Runner's 1/2 kit sits over the rear half of the hardtop on gutter legs, which is why it is sold as a half rack, but Dometic's page does not state panel removal, so ask. A full-length tray or a crossbar set with a bar over the front panels will tie them down."),
 ("How much weight can a Wrangler JL hardtop carry?",
  "We could not confirm a Jeep roof load figure from any Jeep page, so the owner's manual is the authority. What we can give you is the rack makers' numbers. Rhino-Rack rates its RJLB1 Backbone at 264 lb, and ExtremeTerrain lists the JB0880 Backbone kit at 176 lb dynamic. Rough Country rates the 10612 at 225 lb dynamic and 450 lb static. Hooke Road rates its 2-door rack at 160 lb evenly distributed, and TrailFX rates the JL012T at 300 lb. The rack's own weight counts against any dynamic figure, so an 86 lb Front Runner Extreme kit uses far more of your budget than a 25 lb Backbone. Use the lowest number you can find."),
 ("Do roof racks from the 2007–2018 Wrangler JK fit the JL?",
  "Only when the maker says so. The JL went into production in November 2017 and the JK was built until April 27, 2018, so both were sold as 2018 models, and a listing that says only \"2018 Wrangler\" can be for either body. Rhino-Rack sells a separate Backbone for the JL (RJLB1) and the JK (RJKB1), and Front Runner sells separate JK and JL kits. Some crossbar sets are the exception: the 200 lb set and the Grandroad set on this page name the JK, the JL and the Gladiator JT in one title. Look for the letters JL or a year of 2019 or later before you buy."),
 ("What is the difference between a Backbone rack and a gutter-mount rack?",
  "Where the load goes. Rhino-Rack's Backbone is an interior structure, three plates on each side joined by a frame inside the hardtop, and the legs and bars attach through it, which ExtremeTerrain says requires drilling holes through the roof. The rack then carries up to 264 lb by Rhino-Rack's figure because the hardtop shell is reinforced. A gutter-mount kit, such as Front Runner's 1/2 kit with eight gutter-mount legs or Hooke Road's rain-gutter rack, clamps to the hardtop's drip rail with no drilling, which is reversible but limited by the hardtop skin. Pick the Backbone for a tent or heavy gear, and a gutter kit if you want the hardtop unmarked."),
 ("Will a roof rack work with the Wrangler 4xe or the Rubicon 392?",
  "Check each listing. Rough Country's configurator lists the 10612 as compatible with the 4xe. Dometic says the Front Runner Slimline II 1/2 kit is \"Not suitable for 4xe models\". The other makers here do not mention the 4xe or the 392 on the pages we read, so ask before ordering. Both the 4xe and the 392 are 4-door only, which rules out the 2-door picks anyway. Owners of a 2024 or later Jeep should also look at the years in the title: the Rhino-Rack listing stops at 2022 and the crossbar titles at 2024, so later-year owners should confirm with the seller."),
 ("Are the Amazon crossbars and baskets as good as Rhino-Rack or Front Runner?",
  "They publish far less. The 200 lb crossbar set, the Grandroad bars and the SUPAREE basket are described here from their Amazon listing titles only, because amazon.com pages cannot be opened by us and no maker page was found. Rhino-Rack, Dometic, Rough Country and Hooke Road publish a rating, materials, mounting and, for most, a warranty. For a kayak in summer or a cargo box on a trip, a budget set that names your door count and hardtop is a sensible buy if you check the clamps often. For a rooftop tent or gear left on all year, buy a rack with a published rating and a warranty."),
]

